{"name":"Sly Fox","hex":"#804741","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sly fox","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sly or crafty person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sly_fox"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sly Fox","blocks":[{"text":"Sly Fox is a comedic play by Larry Gelbart, based on Ben Jonson's Volpone, updating the setting from Renaissance Venice to 19th century San Francisco, and changing the tone from satire to farce."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sly_Fox","wikidata":"Q17110191"},{"title":"Sly Fox (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Sly Fox was an American new wave music duo, consisting of P-Funk vocalist Gary \"Mudbone\" Cooper and Michael Camacho. The duo came to prominence in the mid-1980s with their UK/US top 10 hit single \"Let's Go All the Way\". They released one studio album of the same name which charted within the US Top 40, and a couple of subsequent singles before breaking up."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sly_Fox_(band)","wikidata":"Q2294786"},{"title":"Fox","blocks":[{"text":"Foxes are small-to-medium-sized omnivorous mammals belonging to several genera of the family Canidae. They have a flattened skull; upright, triangular ears; a pointed, slightly upturned snout; and a long, bushy tail (\"brush\")."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg/330px-Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fox","wikidata":"Q8331"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Vulpes_vulpes_%26_Urocyon_cinereoargenteus_skulls_%26_mandibles.jpg/500px-Vulpes_vulpes_%26_Urocyon_cinereoargenteus_skulls_%26_mandibles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Vulpes_vulpes_%26_Urocyon_cinereoargenteus_skulls_%26_mandibles.jpg/1280px-Vulpes_vu